{
 "source": "High Seas of Mutiny — FINAL.json, supplied by the author, plus the icon set that came with it.",
 "note": "Import record for \"High Seas of Mutiny\", gordy_gordy_gordy's homebrew script, written from the script JSON the author supplied and the 30 icons that came with it. Everything is the author's own: ability, team, night order, night reminders, reminder tokens, setup and the official-schema `special` flags. Nothing else was written, because the source carries no almanac prose — no flavour line, summary, how-to-run or examples — and none was invented. Notes:\n- Four of the names already belong to other creators here (Corsair, Kraken, Mermaid, Stowaway), so those four take a -high-seas-of-mutiny URL in the wiki's existing duplicate style. The other 26 keep their plain slug. Every name is left exactly as the author wrote it, including Umibōzu's macron and the Scurvy Scalawag's \"for for\".\n- The icons are the ones in the author's zip: one per character, the finished set with the white token rim. They go through the site's own 591x591 resize, the same transform as assets/art-normalize.js. The script JSON also links alignment-flipped copies on imgur, but those carry a soft white glow instead of the rim, so putting one in the alternate-art slot would have shown two different icon treatments on the same page. None were used, and the alternate slot is left empty.\n- The night reminders keep the author's wording. Only their tool's markup comes out: \":reminder:\", which is where that tool draws a reminder-token icon, and the asterisks around *YOU ARE*. A night reminder renders here as escaped plain text, so both would have shown up as literal characters.\n- The night order numbers are the author's own, and they are positions within this script (first nights run 2 to 30, other nights 1 to 16) rather than on the official global scale the wiki's night-order picker uses — the Kraken kills at 7 where the Imp is at 40. They therefore sort this script exactly as intended, but do not interleave correctly with official characters in a mixed script.\n- The five Travellers are `traveler` in the source, which is the official schema's spelling; the wiki's team key is `traveller`, so they are stored that way. They also ship a third icon each, which the wiki's two art slots have no room for.\n- The author's background art is the page background for both the script and the collection, and the title lockup cropped out of it is the header on each.\n- The set has no tags and no almanac prose, which would leave all 30 pages Partial and hidden from browsing (assets/classify.js), so the collection carries Starlight - that lends the status to its members and keeps them visible. It is one flag to turn off if that is not wanted.\n- The script JSON's _meta names the author as \"Gordon Fitzgerald\". Every credit here says gordy_gordy_gordy instead, as instructed, so all 30 characters, the script and the collection land on one creator page. No account of that name exists yet, so every row is written with owner_id NULL; an admin can hand them over from the dashboard once there is one.",
